<keyword> 1.1

      .--------------------------------------------------------------.
      | 1.1   About This Documentation                               |
      `--------------------------------------------------------------'

       The MPL documentation and help system are not designed to teach
       theories and programming in general.  It is assumed that most
       people dabbling into MPL have some other type of programming
       experience.  The goal of this documentation is to reference all
       of the MPL syntax and functions, not to teach programming
       itself.

       If MPL is your first try at any type of computer programming,
       it is recommended that you purchase a book on programming in
       Turbo Pascal and download one of the many free Pascal compilers
       found on the Internet.  You may also be able to teach yourself
       by examining and modifying existing MPL programs which can also
       be found on the Internet.

       Also note that at this time, this documentation has not been
       fully completed.

       --------------------------------------------------------------
       <a href=PREVIOUS>Previous Topic</a>                                 <a href=INDEX>Return to Index</a>
<end>

<keyword> 2.0

      .--------------------------------------------------------------.
      | 2.0   Using MPLC: The Command Line Compiler                  |
      `--------------------------------------------------------------'

       MPLC is the Mystic Programming Language command line compiler,
       used for compiling MPL source files (.MPS) from the command line.

       The syntax for using MPLC.EXE is as follows:

       <clr=49>MPLC.EXE [source file mask].MPS<clr=48>

       The source file mask can be any file name or any wildcard file
       name.  The file extention is not required, MPLC will automatically
       append .MPS to the source mask.

       Examples of using MPLC.EXE:

       <clr=49>MPLC.EXE MPSDEMO      - Compiles the source file MPSDEMO.MPS<clr=48>
       <clr=49>MPLC.EXE *            - Compiles all .MPS files in a directory<clr=48>

       --------------------------------------------------------------
       <a href=INDEX>Return to Index</a>
<end>

